WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:13.120
[Narrator:] This is Michael Thompson. He was born 
this morning.

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:18.940
His heritage is good, strong, healthy stock. No evident abnormality.

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:29.300
What kind of person will you be, Michael Thomp... 
has made its impress on you?

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:32.720
What town you will grow up in.

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:38.020
This is the street where you will spend most of your 
early years.

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:42.440
This is the house where you will live.

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:44.580
Your first school.

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:50.680
`And the people, who are the important people in 
your world, Michael Thompson?

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:55.840
There's old Mrs. Radus who lives next door.

00:00:56.040 --> 00:01:02.220
[ Music ]

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.560
She doesn't like children very much.

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:09.540
Then there is Homer Buchanan who lives nearby.

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:13.560
[ Music ]

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:15.320
Homer likes children.

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:17.460
[ Music ]

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:20.840
And there's Mr. Perry the milkman.

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:23.720
[ Music ]

00:01:23.860 --> 00:01:25.880
And Andy the grocery clerk.

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:28.080
[ Music ]

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:30.020
The postman who comes every day.

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:32.840
[ Music ]

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:36.140
And the policeman who directs traffic at the school 
every afternoon.

00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:40.320
[ Music ]

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:42.620
And a whole succession of schoolteachers.

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:51.180
[ Music ]

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:54.480
And children in and out of school.

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:57.540
[ Music ]

00:01:57.540 --> 00:02:00.760
In a few more years, a baby brother.

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:04.620
[ Music ]

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:09.380
And most important of all, your father and mother.

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:12.880
[ Music ]

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:16.700
This is your world, Michael Thompson, and the 
important people in it.

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:23.120
The people who will love you, who will push you 
and pull you, help you and hinder you

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:27.140
in your job of growing to be a man.

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:32.420
Let's look at your world a little closer, Michael, and 
see what it will do to you.

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:37.900
Let's start with your father, Daniel Thompson and 
your mother, Elizabeth Channing Thompson.

00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:43.100
They love you very much, Michael, they want you 
very much.

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:49.480
[Father:] Why, he's so red! There's nothing wrong 
with him, is there?

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:54.160
[Mother:] No. He's a fine boy. I think he's beautiful.

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:55.800
[ Silence ]

00:02:58.460 --> 00:03:03.020
[Narrator:] Yes, they want you very much, Michael, 
and they have definite ideas

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:04.480
of what they want you to be.

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:10.700
Preconceived ideas, dreams that will influence the 
way they act.

00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:15.280
[Father:] Michael, Michael F. Thompson. You're 
going far, son.

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:18.560
[Narrator:] Your father expects big things from you.

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:22.540
He wants you to be better than he is, to grasp the 
opportunities he missed.

00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:25.240
To realize his unfulfilled aspirations.

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:28.340
And your mother expects things too.

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:31.640
She wants you to love her as much as she loves 
you.

00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:37.700
To need her love, to need her care now, and a little 
later, and forever.

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:40.780
Dreams, Michael, all parents have dreams.

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:42.600
Everyone has dreams.

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:45.680
Most of the time they don't even know they have 
them.

00:03:47.720 --> 00:03:53.120
In a few days, they take you home and some of the 
most important days of your life begin.

00:03:53.160 --> 00:04:07.600
[ Music ]

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:10.940
You need a nice, warm world, Michael.

00:04:10.940 --> 00:04:14.400
You need loving care and gentle affection.

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:19.760
You need a happy, secure home and your parents 
give you everything you need, Michael,

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:27.900
gladly and easily, uncritically, because now you are 
exactly what they want, what their dreams want.

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:42.900
[ Music ]

00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:45.320
Everyone knows what a little baby is like.

00:04:45.320 --> 00:04:48.360
Charming, helpless, and appealing.

00:04:48.360 --> 00:04:51.340
Your father and mother know it too, Michael.

00:04:51.340 --> 00:04:53.720
They don't expect you to be anything else.

00:04:53.940 --> 00:05:00.700
[ Music ]

00:05:00.720 --> 00:05:06.220
And then you start to grow up, Michael, and there's 
a wonderful excitement about every new thing.

00:05:06.220 --> 00:05:10.640
Well, about almost every new thing.

00:05:10.640 --> 00:05:16.380
There are some new things that don't quite fit with 
your mother's dream.

00:05:21.140 --> 00:05:26.600
You're growing up now and you don't like to be 
cuddled all the time.

00:05:26.600 --> 00:05:32.460
[Mother:] He never lets me hold him anymore.

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:36.020
Michael, take that dirty thing out of your mouth.

00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:38.780
[Father:] Let him alone. He's growing up.

00:05:38.780 --> 00:05:43.700
[Narrator:] And very often, Michael, the things you 
do, the things every baby does,

00:05:43.700 --> 00:05:47.780
don't always fit in with your father's dream either.

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:54.380
[ Baby is being fed, messily. ]

00:05:58.040 --> 00:06:00.340
[Father:] Does he have to be so messy about it?

00:06:00.340 --> 00:06:02.920
Here, let me feed him.

00:06:02.920 --> 00:06:06.360
[ Silence ]

00:06:06.520 --> 00:06:11.440
Eat. Eat.

00:06:11.840 --> 00:06:16.860
[Mother:] Let him alone, Daniel. He's just a baby.

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:22.840
[Narrator:] First father says let him alone, he's 
growing up,

00:06:22.840 --> 00:06:25.880
and then mother says let him alone he's just a 
baby.

00:06:26.060 --> 00:06:27.900
Why don't they let you alone?

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:31.700
Each of them has a dream about what he wants 
you to be.

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:34.820
Each tries to mold you according to his dream.

00:06:34.820 --> 00:06:41.160
Mother can't let you be independent, father can't 
wait until you're ready to do new things.

00:06:41.360 --> 00:06:42.900
Remember mother's dream?

00:06:42.980 --> 00:06:45.160
She wants you to cling to her forever.

00:06:46.700 --> 00:06:48.900
Remember father's dream?

00:06:49.060 --> 00:06:53.400
He wants you to grow into the ideal he has set for 
you.

00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:59.900
Michael, you're growing up the way you have to 
grow up, doing what you have to do,

00:06:59.900 --> 00:07:07.760
exploring new things, going back to old things, 
even when it's not quite the way your father 
expects it to happen.

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:11.300
Even when it's not the way your mother would like 
it to be.

00:07:11.300 --> 00:07:19.600
Well, Michael, you keep on growing, and as the 
years pass there other times, happy times too,

00:07:19.600 --> 00:07:22.940
many of them, when what you really are comes 
very close

00:07:22.940 --> 00:07:26.120
to what your parents think you should be.

00:07:26.120 --> 00:07:29.080
You've learned to feed yourself pretty well by now.

00:07:29.080 --> 00:07:33.120
A little closer to your father's dream of you.

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:43.500
[ Music ]

00:07:43.500 --> 00:07:50.100
And when it's time for bed and your mother tucks 
you in, you come a little closer to her dream.

00:07:50.100 --> 00:08:01.080
[ Music ]

00:08:01.460 --> 00:08:08.100
Sleep is good, Michael, when you feel secure with 
your parents, when you know they love you.

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:17.360
[ Music ]

00:08:17.840 --> 00:08:24.840
But sometimes when you wake up and the night is 
dark and quiet, you get a little uneasy.

00:08:24.840 --> 00:08:28.580
For little children, there's something strange about 
the night.

00:08:28.580 --> 00:08:31.400
Something unfriendly.

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:52.940
[ Music ]

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:59.160
Even your toys don't comfort you, and you need 
comforting, Michael.

00:08:59.160 --> 00:09:01.300
You want your father and mother.

00:09:01.300 --> 00:09:05.980
Nothing very special or urgent about it, but what 
will happen, Michael?

00:09:05.980 --> 00:09:08.620
Will your father get angry and say...

00:09:08.620 --> 00:09:10.500
[Father:] Get back into bed right this minute.

00:09:10.500 --> 00:09:16.240
[Narrator:] Is that what's going to happen, Michael? 
Or will your mother get her worried look and say...

00:09:16.280 --> 00:09:20.580
[Mother:] My baby. Come to mommy.

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:25.600
[Narrator:] Is that what will happen? Will they make 
more of this moment than is really there?

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:32.040
[ Music ]

00:09:32.300 --> 00:09:37.400
Or does this happen? What ought to happen.

00:09:37.400 --> 00:09:44.440
[ Music ]

00:09:44.440 --> 00:09:48.960
You see, they can modify their dreams, your father 
and mother.

00:09:48.960 --> 00:09:55.160
They can sometimes break away from their fixed 
ideas of what you ought to do and be.

00:09:55.180 --> 00:10:01.720
It seems so easy for them to spend a few moments 
making the night seem warm and friendly again,

00:10:01.720 --> 00:10:04.940
so that you don't mind going back to your room.

00:10:04.940 --> 00:10:12.060
But it isn't easy when mother wants to keep you a 
baby, and father is impatient when you act like a 
baby.

00:10:12.060 --> 00:10:20.100
As a matter of fact, Michael, you're a little of both; 
sometimes a baby and sometimes quite grown-up.

00:10:20.140 --> 00:10:29.360
No, it isn't easy, this business of growing up. It isn't 
easy in the outside world either.

00:10:29.360 --> 00:10:44.060
[ Music ]

00:10:44.060 --> 00:10:51.480
[Woman:] You stay away from my flowers, Michael 
Thompson. Go on. Scoot! Scoot!

00:10:51.480 --> 00:10:55.320
[Narrator:] There is no place in her dreams for 
children.

00:10:55.320 --> 00:11:01.060
Mrs. Radus thinks little boys are horrid monsters 
who want to trample her flowers.

00:11:01.060 --> 00:11:12.060
[ Music ]

00:11:12.060 --> 00:11:14.740
But Homer knows they're not monsters.

00:11:14.740 --> 00:11:19.640
Homer can accept boys and girls pretty much as 
they are and he likes them that way.

00:11:19.640 --> 00:11:23.960
Children don't get in the way of Homer's dreams.

00:11:23.960 --> 00:11:36.560
[ Music ]

00:11:36.560 --> 00:11:40.400
[Michael:] Uncle Homer, look what I found. Boxing 
gloves.

00:11:40.400 --> 00:11:43.800
[Homer:] Oh, fun. Bring them down. Come on. We'll 
put them on.

00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:58.520
[ Music ]

00:11:58.520 --> 00:12:10.160
All right, fellas. Come on, out here. Let's put the 
gloves on. Come on, give me your right one. 
That's it.

00:12:11.360 --> 00:12:14.840
[Narrator:] Children love Homer because he always 
lets them try out new things

00:12:14.840 --> 00:12:18.460
without forgetting that they're still children.

00:12:18.460 --> 00:12:24.540
[Homer:] Come on, hit me, hit me, hard, hard, hard, 
hard, oh.

00:12:24.540 --> 00:12:29.060
[Narrator:] Wonderful man, that Homer.

00:12:29.060 --> 00:12:33.220
That's right, Michael, take it home, that wonderful 
experience.

00:12:33.220 --> 00:12:35.580
Take it home and share it.

00:12:35.600 --> 00:12:37.520
Your father's pleased.

00:12:37.520 --> 00:12:41.440
He understands about these things, but your 
mother is upset because,

00:12:41.440 --> 00:12:45.380
well, she doesn't want you to learn things like 
boxing.

00:12:45.380 --> 00:12:48.860
[Father:] Boxing gloves. Where did you get those 
from, son?

00:12:48.860 --> 00:12:53.680
[Michael:] Uncle Homer gave them to me and he 
showed me how to box and I knocked him down.

00:12:54.260 --> 00:12:59.340
[Father:] Oh, he did, eh? Let's put these on and let 
a real expert show you how to use them.

00:13:00.300 --> 00:13:03.520
[Narrator:] Why does your father have that edge in 
his voice?

00:13:03.520 --> 00:13:09.220
Is he hurt because he wasn't the first to show you?

00:13:09.280 --> 00:13:11.800
[Father:] The first thing to do is to get your position 
right.

00:13:11.800 --> 00:13:15.600
[Narrator:] Why does he have to make this a 
lesson?

00:13:15.600 --> 00:13:19.340
[Father:] Lead with your left and cross with your 
right.

00:13:19.340 --> 00:13:22.460
Go on, cross with your right.

00:13:23.160 --> 00:13:27.120
Now the main thing is to keep moving all the time, 
keep jabbing, keep coming in.

00:13:27.120 --> 00:13:29.780
Keep your guard up.

00:13:29.780 --> 00:13:32.740
You're wide open now; jab with your right.

00:13:32.740 --> 00:13:38.040
Watch your chin; got to learn to defend yourself. 
Watch it now.

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:41.980
[ Child crying ]

00:13:41.980 --> 00:13:48.280
[Narrator:] No, it isn't easy to grow up, Michael, 
especially when your father expects

00:13:48.280 --> 00:13:54.200
so much of you, when he's got a dream he wants 
very much to come true,

00:13:54.200 --> 00:13:57.500
and it doesn't quite come true for your dreams 
either, Michael.

00:13:57.500 --> 00:14:02.680
[Mother:] In a few weeks now, Michael, mommy is 
going to the same hospital where she had you.

00:14:02.680 --> 00:14:05.860
You remember, the building with the white pillars.

00:14:05.860 --> 00:14:08.660
And she's going to have a little baby for you to 
play with.

00:14:08.660 --> 00:14:11.700
[Father:] That's right, Mike, then you'll have a 
brother to play ball with.

00:14:11.700 --> 00:14:13.940
[Mother:] Don't say that, Daniel, it might be a girl.

00:14:13.940 --> 00:14:16.400
[Father:] Nonsense. It'll be a boy and we'll name 
him Robin.

00:14:16.400 --> 00:14:22.000
[Mother:] You're so sure of yourself. Why, ever 
since I've played with dolls I've wanted a girl baby.

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:24.300
[Father:] Dolls, don't be silly, Elizabeth.

00:14:24.300 --> 00:14:28.820
Wait 'til you see him, Mike. You can teach him to 
ride your bike and box with him.

00:14:28.820 --> 00:14:31.860
[Mother:] All you think about is boxing, boxing.

00:14:31.860 --> 00:14:35.900
Remember the white pillars, remember the white 
pillars, remember the white pillars, remember the

00:14:35.900 --> 00:14:41.340
white pillars, remember the white pillars, remember 
the white pillars.

00:14:41.340 --> 00:14:45.000
Play with dolls. Play with dolls. Play with dolls.

00:14:45.000 --> 00:14:49.200
[Father:] Don't be silly, don't be silly, don't be silly, 
don't be silly, don't be silly.

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:54.480
Box with him, box with him, box with him, box with 
him, box with him, box with him, box with him.

00:14:54.480 --> 00:14:57.380
[Mother:] Boxing, boxing, boxing, boxing.

00:14:57.380 --> 00:15:00.300
[Father:] Why do you keep harping on that?

00:15:00.300 --> 00:15:02.960
[Mother:] You're just confusing the boy saying 
things like that.

00:15:02.960 --> 00:15:05.260
[Father:] Of course, Mike, you'll have to share your 
toys with him,

00:15:05.260 --> 00:15:07.960
but you won't mind that because you've got lots of 
toys.

00:15:07.960 --> 00:15:10.920
[Mother:] I don't know why you do it, Daniel, I really 
don't.

00:15:10.920 --> 00:15:13.960
[Michael:] I don't want a brother.

00:15:13.960 --> 00:15:17.240
[Narrator:] For children the difference between 
dreams and reality is very slight.

00:15:17.240 --> 00:15:21.400
So slight that when the baby brother actually 
comes, Michael isn't very sure.

00:15:21.400 --> 00:15:25.080
[Mother:] Be careful, Michael. He's very delicate.

00:15:25.080 --> 00:15:27.260
[Father:] Mustn't touch the baby, son.

00:15:27.260 --> 00:15:29.100
[Michael:] Is that my brother, mommy?

00:15:29.100 --> 00:15:31.240
[Mother:] Yes, Michael.

00:15:31.240 --> 00:15:32.600
[Michael:] He's so little.

00:15:32.600 --> 00:15:35.960
[Father:] What did you expect? Someone as big as 
you?

00:15:35.960 --> 00:15:39.360
[ Music ]

00:15:42.620 --> 00:15:45.280
[Narrator:] What did you expect, Michael?

00:15:45.280 --> 00:15:48.960
Someone as big and frightening as your 
daydream?

00:15:48.960 --> 00:15:53.080
[ Music ]

00:15:54.840 --> 00:15:59.120
He cries when you touch him.

00:15:59.660 --> 00:16:06.320
[Father:] Michael, let that baby alone.

00:16:12.940 --> 00:16:16.600
[Narrator:] He's so little, but he can get you in 
trouble.

00:16:16.600 --> 00:16:20.360
You think he'll always get you in trouble.

00:16:20.360 --> 00:16:22.680
You think he must be your enemy.

00:16:22.680 --> 00:16:28.400
Will your frightening dream always make him your 
enemy even when you're both a little bigger?

00:16:28.400 --> 00:16:36.300
[ Music ]

00:16:36.300 --> 00:16:41.220
Will he still be your enemy a few years later?

00:16:41.220 --> 00:16:43.320
[Michael:] You stay here. I'm going to go play ball.

00:16:43.320 --> 00:16:45.700
[Child:] You better take me with you or I'll tell 
mommy.

00:16:45.700 --> 00:16:48.780
[Michael:] Don't you dare.

00:16:48.780 --> 00:16:53.840
[Narrator:] That's the way it can be, Michael, when 
you have a preconceived idea about something,

00:16:53.840 --> 00:16:56.300
about someone.

00:16:56.300 --> 00:16:58.120
That's the way it is with everyone.

00:16:58.120 --> 00:17:02.820
Without our even knowing it, we try to make things 
happen the way we expect them to happen.

00:17:02.820 --> 00:17:08.320
That's the way it is with your parents, too, with your 
mother trying to make you into her dream.

00:17:08.320 --> 00:17:11.360
[ Music ]

00:17:11.360 --> 00:17:14.340
With your father trying to make you like his dream.

00:17:14.500 --> 00:17:20.660
They really don't want the same boy and you can't 
make either dream come true.

00:17:20.660 --> 00:17:23.520
It never happens that way.

00:17:23.520 --> 00:17:27.080
Let's see what it might be like, Michael, if your 
mother's dream

00:17:27.080 --> 00:17:29.260
were the chief influence in your life.

00:17:29.260 --> 00:17:34.860
Your mother who protects you too much, who 
worries too much.

00:17:34.860 --> 00:17:38.020
[ Silence ]

00:17:38.020 --> 00:17:41.920
Who can't bear to let you grow up, to grow away 
from her.

00:17:41.920 --> 00:17:50.060
After a while you even feel guilty about growing up.

00:17:50.060 --> 00:17:55.800
[Mother:] Oh, my, just think that my boy is big 
enough for a suit like that.

00:17:55.800 --> 00:17:59.200
You don't think it's too old-looking for him?

00:18:02.020 --> 00:18:05.720
[Michael:] Gee whiz, mom. You've gotta let me grow 
up sometime.

00:18:05.780 --> 00:18:11.000
[Narrator:] Yes, Michael, she's got to let you grow 
up, but she'll do it grudgingly, unwillingly.

00:18:11.400 --> 00:18:17.100
It's the new things like your first long pants that 
make her feel lonely and old.

00:18:17.680 --> 00:18:20.100
She doesn't want to lose you.

00:18:20.100 --> 00:18:26.160
Every new thing, every first time is a threat, an 
attack aimed at her dream.

00:18:26.160 --> 00:18:29.360
[Father:] How does it feel going to your first dance, 
son?

00:18:29.360 --> 00:18:31.480
[Michael:] Oh, all right I guess.

00:18:31.480 --> 00:18:33.500
[Father:] Taking a girl?

00:18:33.500 --> 00:18:36.540
[Michael:] Not exactly.

00:18:36.540 --> 00:18:38.700
[Narrator:] No, he's not taking a girl.

00:18:38.700 --> 00:18:41.960
Why do you feel so troubled, Michael?

00:18:41.960 --> 00:18:46.820
Is it because you know that you're not really what 
your mother wants you to be?

00:18:46.820 --> 00:18:50.180
Her baby boy?

00:18:50.180 --> 00:18:52.900
Oh, you'll go out with girls before very long.

00:18:52.900 --> 00:18:56.520
[ Music ]

00:18:56.520 --> 00:18:59.480
But you won't be happy about it.

00:18:59.480 --> 00:19:07.100
[ Music ]

00:19:07.100 --> 00:19:13.080
You'll get married too but no matter whom you 
marry there won't be much joy in it.

00:19:13.080 --> 00:19:20.640
Women make you feel guilty, all women, just the 
way your mother makes you feel guilty.

00:19:21.300 --> 00:19:26.620
Yes, Michael, that's the way it would be with your 
mother's dream running things.

00:19:26.620 --> 00:19:30.400
Let's suppose instead of your mother's dream 
dominating, things happen,

00:19:30.400 --> 00:19:35.620
things always happen the way your father's dream 
forces them to happen.

00:19:35.620 --> 00:19:38.420
Remember that night you woke up a little 
frightened?

00:19:41.420 --> 00:19:45.420
[Father:] Get back into bed. Get back into bed 
right this minute.

00:19:45.540 --> 00:19:46.920
[Narrator:] And that day Mrs. Radus chased you?

00:19:46.920 --> 00:19:48.620
[Father:] Stop sucking your thumb.

00:19:48.620 --> 00:19:51.380
[Narrator:] Remember when your new brother 
arrived?

00:19:51.380 --> 00:19:54.420
[Father:] Michael, let that baby alone. You ought to 
have better sense than that.

00:19:54.700 --> 00:20:00.600
[Narrator:] You see, Michael, it isn't that your father 
doesn't love you; it's just that he expects too much.

00:20:01.120 --> 00:20:04.940
[Michael:] Goodbye, mom, goodbye pop.

00:20:04.940 --> 00:20:07.320
[Father:] Michael, come back here.

00:20:07.320 --> 00:20:10.100
[Michael:] But, pop, we want to go swimming.

00:20:10.100 --> 00:20:12.160
[Father:] Come here when I call you.

00:20:12.420 --> 00:20:14.420
What do you mean slamming that door that way?

00:20:14.440 --> 00:20:16.000
Haven't you got any better manners than that?

00:20:16.000 --> 00:20:19.180
[Michael:] But, pop, I was late.

00:20:19.180 --> 00:20:21.320
[Father:] Don't answer back that way.

00:20:21.320 --> 00:20:23.100
Have you cleaned up your room?

00:20:23.100 --> 00:20:24.660
[Michael:] But, pop.

00:20:24.660 --> 00:20:26.340
[Father:] Be quiet. Now go upstairs and clean up 
that mess.

00:20:29.140 --> 00:20:35.600
[Narrator:] It isn't easy with a father who won't ever 
listen to you, who is never satisfied.

00:20:36.820 --> 00:20:40.080
[Father:] I know he wants to go swimming, but 
we've got to teach him responsibility.

00:20:40.080 --> 00:20:43.880
[Narrator:] Responsibility. Yes, he wants you to 
have all the virtues, Michael.

00:20:43.880 --> 00:20:47.880
He wants you to be the strongest, the finest, the 
best of all.

00:20:48.040 --> 00:20:56.380
[ Kid's playing ]

00:20:56.920 --> 00:20:59.220
[Michael:] Yippee, we won.

00:20:59.220 --> 00:21:03.180
[Narrator:] It's a good feeling when you win, 
Michael, when you're on the winning side.

00:21:03.180 --> 00:21:05.180
Your father should be pleased.

00:21:05.180 --> 00:21:12.020
[Michael:] Pop, hey, pop, we won 8 to 5 and 
Johnny got a home run and a three-bagger.

00:21:12.020 --> 00:21:13.760
[Father:] How many did you get, son?

00:21:13.760 --> 00:21:18.520
[Michael:] I got a two-bagger and a couple of 
singles.

00:21:18.560 --> 00:21:20.980
[Father:] Well, better luck next time.

00:21:22.820 --> 00:21:24.980
[Narrator:] Never satisfied. Always wants you a little 
different, a little better.

00:21:26.720 --> 00:21:28.160
More like his dream.

00:21:28.960 --> 00:21:32.360
But you don't know about his dream, Michael, and 
you're all [?]

00:21:32.360 --> 00:21:33.700
Sooner or later you stop trying.

00:21:33.700 --> 00:21:36.880
That's why you avoid those school dances.

00:21:37.100 --> 00:21:39.600
You want to go but you're afraid.

00:21:39.960 --> 00:21:42.740
You'll come close but you won't go in.

00:21:42.740 --> 00:21:49.280
It's hard to do anything when your father is always 
saying don't do this, don't do that, be the best.

00:21:50.180 --> 00:21:52.740
[Boy:] Why don't you look where you're going?

00:21:52.740 --> 00:21:57.460
[Narrator:] He's wrong but he makes you feel the 
way you do with your father, afraid.

00:21:57.460 --> 00:22:01.500
A sharp tone of voice, a disapproving attitude, a 
person in authority.

00:22:01.500 --> 00:22:07.780
Any one of them can make you feel afraid, angry, 
resentful.

00:22:07.780 --> 00:22:17.020
[ Music ]

00:22:17.160 --> 00:22:20.480
After a while it won't even have to be your father,

00:22:20.480 --> 00:22:25.360
or anyone outside of yourself that makes you feel 
that way.

00:22:25.360 --> 00:22:31.080
[ Music ]

00:22:31.080 --> 00:22:35.260
[Woman:] Oh, I'm so sorry.

00:22:38.280 --> 00:22:40.780
[Man:] Hiya, Mike. Well, didja get the raise?

00:22:40.780 --> 00:22:42.300
[Michael:] Nah, I quit.

00:22:42.300 --> 00:22:44.500
[Man:] Quit? Why? What did he do?

00:22:44.500 --> 00:22:46.000
[Michael:] Do?

00:22:46.140 --> 00:22:48.840
[ Music ]

00:22:48.840 --> 00:22:52.720
He didn't do anything. I didn't give him a chance; I 
quit first.

00:22:52.720 --> 00:22:57.280
[Narrator:] Not very pretty is it, Michael, either way; 
mama's boy or papa's boy.

00:22:59.200 --> 00:23:02.560
They wouldn't like you to turn out either way, your 
father and mother,

00:23:02.560 --> 00:23:06.420
even though it would be their dreams that helped 
to make it that way.

00:23:06.420 --> 00:23:13.160
But let's go back, back to the hospital on that first 
day when the nurse took you to your parents.

00:23:13.160 --> 00:23:34.140
[ Music ]

00:23:34.560 --> 00:23:39.780
It doesn't have to happen that way, Michael, either 
way because your parents can break away from

00:23:39.780 --> 00:23:45.300
the rigid patterns of their dreams or at least they 
can learn to hold them back a little.

00:23:45.580 --> 00:23:49.780
Your father and mother don't have to be perfect to 
be good parents; they can learn that

00:23:49.780 --> 00:23:54.740
only by bringing up a child--you, Michael--for your 
own sake,

00:23:54.740 --> 00:23:58.360
can they get the kind of grownup son they want.

00:23:58.360 --> 00:24:04.180
With parents who help you mature properly and 
fully, you'll have a warm, secure baby world

00:24:04.180 --> 00:24:07.340
where you are protected and loved and cared for.

00:24:08.040 --> 00:24:14.460
A world where you are free to follow the gradual, 
inevitable path to manhood at your own pace,

00:24:14.460 --> 00:24:18.900
and with the sympathetic and understanding help 
of your parents, Michael,

00:24:18.900 --> 00:24:22.140
you can succeed in overcoming childhood fears.

00:24:22.140 --> 00:24:27.060
You can avoid having any preconceived ideas that 
your brother is going to be your enemy.

00:24:27.240 --> 00:24:31.600
[ Music ]

00:24:31.860 --> 00:24:36.540
It's difficult for a small boy to understand what a 
new baby is going to be,

00:24:36.540 --> 00:24:39.400
and it's natural for him to be a little curious.

00:24:39.400 --> 00:24:44.920
[ Baby crying ]

00:24:44.920 --> 00:24:51.040
Of course he cries when you touch him and you're 
distressed, but your father will explain things.

00:24:52.920 --> 00:24:57.160
[Father:] Your brother's a little young to play with 
just now.

00:24:57.160 --> 00:25:00.120
We sort of have to take care of him for a while, you 
and I.

00:25:00.120 --> 00:25:02.740
You wait until he gets a little older.

00:25:02.740 --> 00:25:07.280
[Narrator:] With your parents' loving guidance, you 
can learn to accept your brother.

00:25:09.160 --> 00:25:12.920
To accept him as a friend, an equal.

00:25:12.920 --> 00:25:19.680
[ Music ]

00:25:21.280 --> 00:25:25.720
With parents who can modify their own dreams to 
fit your needs,

00:25:25.720 --> 00:25:31.160
you can lead a happy and productive life well- 
equipped to make your way in the world.

00:25:31.220 --> 00:25:35.980
[ Music ]

00:25:36.060 --> 00:25:38.200
[Boy:] Hi, Mike, how you doing?

00:25:38.240 --> 00:25:41.400
[Narrator:] Well-equipped to make your way in your 
world.

00:25:41.400 --> 00:25:42.840
[Boy:] He can't play; he's too little.

00:25:43.100 --> 00:25:45.820
[Michael:] He's not too little. He's my brother.

00:25:46.440 --> 00:25:49.180
[Narrator:] Maybe he is really too little, but Michael,

00:25:49.200 --> 00:25:51.840
you carry some weight in your childhood 
community.

00:25:51.840 --> 00:25:53.560
They accept your judgment.

00:25:53.560 --> 00:25:58.120
You're a person in your own right, Michael, grown 
and matured in an atmosphere of

00:25:58.120 --> 00:26:00.020
love and mutual respect.

00:26:00.160 --> 00:26:05.820
An atmosphere that encourages you to go forward 
joyously to manhood and maturity.

00:26:05.820 --> 00:26:10.980
[ Music ]

00:26:10.980 --> 00:26:15.580
An atmosphere that prepares you to find your 
place in the world with confidence

00:26:15.580 --> 00:26:18.500
and the best use of your abilities.

00:26:18.520 --> 00:26:25.020
[ Music ]

00:26:25.220 --> 00:26:32.080
You can be a well-integrated man, Michael, a whole man, well-qualified to take your place

00:26:32.080 --> 00:26:37.980
in the family, the community, the world.

00:26:37.980 --> 00:26:43.480
You see, there are three Michael Thompsons and 
probably even more.

00:26:43.480 --> 00:26:48.040
Those other two and this one.

00:26:49.040 --> 00:26:56.920
One of them will be you, Michael, the others will-o'- 
the-wisps, might-have-beens.

00:26:56.920 --> 00:27:25.000
[ Music ]

